lly colloquially people divide  them into hard skills and soft skills  when in fact there's actually  way more buckets than just that in my  opinion like the ability  for instance to be able to read  technical documentation and make sense  of it is a very  important software engineering skill  especially as you get more senior and  there aren't answers of stack overflow  things everywhere so  that's one thing especially when i'm  working with editing software  when i'm like reading about anything new  that is written by  academia or anyone like that being able  to get information that way i think is  a really important part of my job  currently being able to google  everything like getting really good at  googling is something that i developed  as a software engineer  and literally like being my own boss and  like not really having  like somebody else who could do my job  means that i'm the  only person sometimes you can figure out  how to do what i want to do which means  it's a lot of googling another skill  that i've been really thankful for  that i use in my day-to-day is just like  project planning and project management  because i'm not sure if you know this  but like in content creation  everything is like a project a video is  a project there's multiple steps  to get it from conceptualization to like  pushing to broad basically which is  youtube as well as just like  making newsletters going live on twitch  like there's so many  things to do all the time and because  i'm my own boss a lot of the time i'm  doing all of it  and so in order to stay organized  literally i still  do sprints i still run my day  and work in sprints and tasks and  prioritize all the lists of tasks and  stuff and that's a very like  i brought that exactly from scrum days  you know one other really important  skill that i  learned as a software engineer that i  use often is my collaboration skills  like even though i work for myself by  myself i still collaborate with many  people  granted it's not like we all work for  the same company or something and it's a  lot of like strangers on the internet  but it's all about just like  getting people to work on something with  you to make something  and that's that's basically software  engineering and coding so yeah i think  the silicon valley mentality has  followed me  in being organized in collaboration so  it's like  setting up meetings while in advance  creating agendas for the meetings  creating  action items for those meetings  following up in those meetings  trying to find alignment and a common  ground in communication with another  person  whose background you have no idea about  and related to that is like writing good  documentation for other people to read  writing good emails being able to manage  like good relationships and  foster good relationships with  collaborators  all of that like all of that are lessons  that i learned as a software engineer  kind of like how hey if i'm gonna do you  a favor  i kind of expect at some point for you  to do me a favor like all of that stuff  is like so incredibly important in  content creation  and so that's been really interesting oh  and one other thing that's been super  helpful  is literally like debugging like i still  debug in my day-to-day  pretty often especially when premiere  pro is being like super difficult to  work with or when i'm trying to get down  to  the bottom of any sort of issue whether  that be like with merch  or with youtube or with any technology  ever because being a content creator  still means using a lot of digital  products just the building blocks are  different  so yeah i think what i learned from not  coding professionally for a full year  is that it just required me to have a  different perspective  about myself my work my skills  my confidence it wasn't easy but  honestly everything considered i'm happy  that i  did what i did and frankly it's quite  scary to post a video on the internet  about this because i am really worried  about what people think  and so i hope that you'll still follow  along with me  in my journey and subscribe to my  channel because  i don't know i still feel like there's a  lot of other things to talk about  within the world of tech that isn't just  coding  to me coding is a tool it's not the  end-all be-all  of everything it's just a tool similar  to like how  a saw is to a carpenter it's one tool  that you use  to get what you want done and it does  unlock a lot of capabilities  because it's cool and ever evolving and  a lot of people are working on it but  there is just so much more to the world  of tech that  i want to talk about so i hope you  indulge me in that  and you don't think of me as a complete  fraud  i sure hope you don't think that thank  you for watching my musings  that come right off the top of my head i  appreciate you all for being here and  watching my videos  because you'll give me purpose in the  work that i do  and validate that it's okay to like live  your life the way that you want to  and that's very very reassuring so  thank you all so much every single  person who watches  my videos leaves nice comments watches  my twitch streams buys merch  joins my youtube membership club like i  feel nothing but  just immense gratitude for all of you in  following along in my journey so thank  you i have  big amazing things in store this year  and i cannot wait to tell you all about  them  so stay tuned i guess like in all of  this  while it's scary and everything makes me  fearful usually still because you know  what your girl has anxiety i am still  very much excited about the future and  what's to come  and yeah i don't know where i'm headed i  don't know what i'm gonna do but  i'm realizing that sometimes that's just  way more exciting and that's not a scary  thing  and i'm coming around to that all right  everybody i'll see you in the next one  bye
 

